From: fp5-touch <local>
Subject: [PATCH] input: focus/activate element on first touch down

TouchDown delivered wl_touch.down to the surface under the finger but never
changed keyboard focus, unlike PointerButton press. On a touch-only device this
means tapping a window does not activate/raise it and text (incl. OSK input)
keeps going to the previously focused surface.

Mirror the pointer path: on the first contact of a touch sequence, when no
move/resize/popup grab owns touch, set keyboard focus to element_under().

Base: cosmic-comp epoch-1.8.0 (a5578599). Type-checked with rustc 1.91
(--ignore-rust-version) on x86_64; not yet run on hardware.
---
diff --git a/src/input/mod.rs b/src/input/mod.rs
index 45586b03..b19f7c31 100644
--- a/src/input/mod.rs
+++ b/src/input/mod.rs
@@ -1463,10 +1463,27 @@ impl State {
                     let under = State::surface_under(position, &output, &shell)
                         .map(|(target, pos)| (target, pos.as_logical()));
 
+                    // Touch-to-focus, mirroring the pointer-press path: activate and give
+                    // keyboard focus to the element under the first finger of a sequence.
+                    // `is_grabbed()` is false only before the first contact (smithay installs
+                    // an implicit TouchDownGrab on it) and when no move/resize/popup grab owns
+                    // touch, so extra fingers and grabbed sequences never steal focus.
+                    // Resize forks are excluded like on the pointer path.
+                    let touch = seat.get_touch().unwrap();
+                    let focus_target = if touch.is_grabbed()
+                        || matches!(under, Some((PointerFocusTarget::ResizeFork(_), _)))
+                    {
+                        None
+                    } else {
+                        State::element_under(position, &output, &shell, &seat)
+                    };
+
                     std::mem::drop(shell);
 
                     let serial = SERIAL_COUNTER.next_serial();
-                    let touch = seat.get_touch().unwrap();
+                    if let Some(target) = focus_target {
+                        Shell::set_focus(self, Some(&target), &seat, Some(serial), false);
+                    }
                     touch.down(
                         self,
                         under,
